---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import Text from '../components/Text.astro';
import { booking, extras } from '../config/booking';
import { site } from '../config/site';

// The page date is the terms version, so what a guest agreed to (bookings.terms_version) matches what's shown here.
// Bump booking.termsVersion whenever anything below changes.
const pounds = (pence: number) => `£${pence / 100}`;
const days = booking.freeCancellationDays;
---

<Legal
  title="Booking terms"
  description={`The terms for booking a ${site.name} home direct: payment, cancellation, check-in and looking after the home.`}
  updated={booking.termsVersion}
  intro="These terms and our house rules are the agreement between you and us when you book on this website. Please read them before you book."
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName}, registered in England and Wales, company no. <Text text={site.companyNumber} />. Registered office: <Text
      text={site.registeredOffice}
    />.
  </p>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>{site.phoneHref ? <>, phone <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a></> : ''}.
    In these terms, "we" and "us" means {site.legalName}. "You" means the person making the booking, who must be one of the guests.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Making a booking</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You must be 18 or over and staying in the home yourself.</li>
    <li>
      You can book up to {booking.maxInstantNights} nights on the website. Your booking is confirmed when your payment goes through and
      we email you a confirmation with your booking reference.
    </li>
    <li>
      Sometimes the website takes a booking request instead of a payment. A request doesn't reserve the dates and costs nothing. We
      reply by email, and the booking is only confirmed once you have paid using the payment link we send.
    </li>
    <li>
      Stays of {booking.maxInstantNights + 1} to {booking.maxNights} nights are booked by enquiry. We send a quote and a short booking
      agreement to sign. Where that agreement differs from these terms, the agreement applies. We don't take stays longer than {
        booking.maxNights
      } nights.
    </li>
    <li>Check your confirmation email and tell us straight away if anything in it is wrong.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Price and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The total shown before you pay is the full price: the nightly rates plus any extras you choose. There is no booking fee, cleaning
      fee or other charge added later. Prices are in pounds sterling.
    </li>
    <li>You pay in full when you book, by card, Apple Pay or Google Pay. Payments are handled by Stripe, so we never see your card details.</li>
    <li>We don't take a security deposit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Extras</h3>
  <ul>
    {
      extras.map((e) => (
        <li>
          {e.label}, {pounds(e.price)} per {e.per}. {e.description}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p>Once you have paid for an extra, it is part of your booking and we will provide it.</p>

  <h2>4. What your booking gives you</h2>
  <p>
    Your booking lets you and the guests named on it stay in the home for a holiday or work trip on the dates booked. It is a licence to
    occupy, not a tenancy, and your main home must be somewhere else. It gives you no right to stay past your checkout date.
  </p>

  <h2>5. If you cancel</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>More than {days} days before check-in:</strong> full refund, including extras. The free cancellation window closes at {
        booking.checkInTime
      } UK time, {days} days before your arrival date. Your confirmation email shows the exact date.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Within {days} days of check-in, or if you don't arrive:</strong> no refund. If you need to cancel late, get in touch anyway
      and we'll see what we can do, but we can't promise a refund.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Leaving early:</strong> no refund for nights you don't use.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can cancel yourself on the <a href="/booking">manage booking</a> page with your booking reference and email, or by emailing us.
    Refunds go back to the card you paid with. Your bank usually shows them within 5 to 10 working days.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Consumer Contracts Regulations 2013 give a 14-day right to cancel many things bought online. That right does not apply to
    accommodation booked for specific dates, so the cancellation terms above apply instead.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Changing your booking</h2>
  <p>
    Email us if you want to change your dates or the number of guests. We'll make the change if the home is free, and you pay or are
    refunded the difference in price. We can't promise a change will be possible.
  </p>

  <h2>7. If we have to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    We'll only cancel if we have to: for example, if the same nights were booked elsewhere at the same moment as yours, or if something
    outside our control (such as a flood or a serious fault) means the home can't be used. If that happens we'll tell you as soon as we
    can and refund everything you paid in full.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Check-in and checkout</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check-in is from {booking.checkInTime} and checkout is by {booking.checkOutTime}, unless you've booked early check-in or late checkout.</li>
    <li>
      Check-in is self check-in with a key lockbox. We email the address, the lockbox code and directions 48 hours before you arrive, so
      make sure the email address and mobile number on your booking are right.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. Looking after the home</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Our <a href="/house-rules">house rules</a> are part of these terms.</li>
    <li>Only the number of guests on your booking may stay, and never more than the home sleeps. You can't sublet or pass the booking to anyone else.</li>
    <li>
      Tell us about any damage or breakage as soon as it happens. If you or your group damage the home or its contents beyond normal
      wear and tear, we'll send you photos and the cost of the repair or replacement, and ask you to pay it.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you or your group seriously break the house rules (for example, by holding a party, bringing more guests than booked or smoking
      in the flat), we may ask you to leave without a refund.
    </li>
    <li>
      We won't come into the home during your stay without arranging it with you first, except in an emergency or to deal with an
      urgent problem such as a leak.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>10. Problems during your stay</h2>
  <p>
    If something isn't right, tell us straight away by email{site.phoneHref ? ', phone or WhatsApp' : ''} and we'll put it right as quickly
    as we can. It is much easier to fix a problem while you're there than after you've left.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Our responsibility to you</h2>
  <p>
    We are responsible for loss or damage you suffer that is a foreseeable result of us breaking these terms or failing to use reasonable
    care and skill. We are not responsible for loss that wasn't foreseeable, or for business losses such as lost profit.
  </p>
  <p>
    We aren't responsible for loss of or damage to your belongings unless it's caused by our negligence. Nothing in these terms limits
    our liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for anything else the law doesn't allow us to
    limit. None of this affects your legal rights as a consumer.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Your information</h2>
  <p>We use your details to manage your booking. Our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains what we keep and why.</p>

  <h2>13. Complaints and the law</h2>
  <p>
    If you're unhappy with anything, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we'll do our best to put it right. These terms
    are governed by the law of England and Wales. You can bring a claim in the courts of England and Wales, or in Scotland or Northern
    Ireland if you live there.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. Your booking is covered by the version you agreed to when you booked. This is version {booking.termsVersion}.
  </p>
</Legal>
